content:
@BenWestgate_ @Abuamerican Not tried Sema but Tirzepatide nuked my appetite beyond comprehension. 

Game changer for obese people but if you’re relatively fit just wanting a cheat code it’s not worth it 

Struggled to eat 800 cals per day

@RockAppleWood @DoctorTro Was keto for 4 plus years. Intermittent fasting as well. Weight and A1c continued to creep. 
Eating the same now. But with mounjaro. Down 65 pounds. 
Also sleeping thru the night for the first time in a decade. Another bonus.

@DrBrandonPettke Yesterday I watched a Youtube video on how Charles Barkley lost so much weight through intermittent fasting and the drug Mounjaro.

I was so intrigued and planned to research it in detail later.

Thanks for this thread Dr. You saved me from that work and shared good advice.

"This is not a quick fix for a celebrity looking to lose ten pounds," @kavitapmd says of new diabetes drug tirzepatide, aka Mounjaro. 

"These drugs are a life changer and truly a life saver for my diabetic patients."

@jdbalart 
@MSNBC https://t.co/mcdV7PdVyf

@thatsnotmine125 @ProfKarolSikora I am referring to the type 2 diabetes medication (that's all the rave now) used for curbing appetite.

That specific use needs to be maintained.  Once stopped, weight gain comes right back.

Some of drugs are Ozempic and Mounjaro as examples.

@FatEmperor 

Nationwide shortage of drugs like Mounjaro, Ozempic, etc. Why aren't doctors prescribing no carb?

I've lost more weight (I was NEVER obese) faster, healthier, &amp; cheaper than ANY of my patients on these "wonder" injections by going BBBE (beef, bacon, butter, &amp;eggs).

People who took Tirzepatide (a drug) lost up to 22% of their body weight and achieved far greater weight loss on average than the placebo group.
@Gizmodo
 https://t.co/rlYXC7ZWsb

People who took Tirzepatide (a drug) lost up to 22% of their body weight and achieved far greater weight loss on average than the placebo group.
@Gizmodo
 https://t.co/UpKoGdpnvH

@RuxandraTeslo I lost 40lb on tirzepatide (Mounjaro)

Idk why there are so many haters tbh, I don’t lie about it

Anytime anyone asks me I’m very honest that I just take a drug and it works, I don’t do “stolen valor” fitness edition claiming some other account of the weight loss

People who took Tirzepatide (a drug) lost up to 22% of their body weight and achieved far greater weight loss on average than the placebo group.
@Gizmodo
 https://t.co/9rJ11Y6tml

@723Magnus @biodiversityge1 I was put on Mounjaro for type2 diabetes in August 
It was $1200.00 with my insurance bc of my high deductible. I changed insurance policies  bc I’ll be on this for life. Now it’s 20 dollars. My sugars are controlled , my A1c is almost normal. 
and I’ve lost 28 pounds 18weeks https://t.co/Dn09l4Cy86

@ScottAdamsSays Mounjaro. Just started dose course Saturday. Preliminary indications are promising. Glucose levels are more stable than Ozempic meaning no up and down glucose spiking.   
  My appetite is also stabilized meaning no urgent hunger pains. 
  No GI distress so far.

@DefiningWealth I ate 1400 cals a day for year and only gained.

I have thyroid disease, PCOS, and PPMD, all which cause weight gain.

Started taking Mounjaro and it’s been a lifesaver. I’m now down 15 pounds, with the same habits I had before.

@KayannaStardust @SilverSapphire9 Same!
The only reason I've been able to qualify for mounjaro is because I'm technically type 1 and type 2. 

It's been wonders for my sugar levels and appetite. I went from using 150 units ever 3 days to needing about 60 units every 3 days in my pod.

@StockMKTNewz As someone in healthcare, This is not surprising. Eli Lilly has been successful with it’s insulin offerings

And now, it has a blockbuster in weight loss in MOUNJARO. 

We cannot stay stocked on mounjaro. And patients come back and tell me they have lost 15-30% total weight.
